{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"mazie","id":"366565198284324868","is_bot":0,"username":"damnzam"},"author_id":"366565198284324868","channel_id":"850783697946804234","content":"> !beyond [link]\n> !gsheet [link]\n> !dicecloud [link]\nUploads your character sheet to Avrae, depending on the source.\n\n> !update\nReloads your character. Use this command when you make changes to your sheet (levelling up, etc), otherwise Avrae won't see them.\n\n> !roll [dice]\nRolls what you tell it to, plain and simple. Anything you type after the dice becomes the title of the roll. Can be abbreviated to !r. \n\n> !check [skill]\nRolls an ability check. Initiative is rolled with this command. Can be abbreviated to !c.\n\n> !attack [name]\nRolls an attack and damage roll using one of the attacks listed in your character sheet. Type !attack without anything afterward to see a list of your attacks. Can be abbreviated to !a.\n\n> !save [ability]\nRolls a saving throw of the chosen ability score. Can be abbreviated to !s.\n\n> !spell [name]\nLooks up a spell and tells you everything about it.\n\n> !game hp [number]\nAdds the number to your HP. Type a negative number to subtract HP when you take damage.\n\n> !game thp [number]\nSame as above except with temporary hit points.\n\n> !game spellslot [level] [number]\nAdds or expends a number spell slots of the chosen level. Type !game spellslot with nothing afterward to view your spell slots. Can be abbreviated to !g ss.\n\n> !game deathsave [reset]\nRolls a death saving throw and keeps track of them. Type 'reset' after the command to wipe your death saves instead of making one. Can be abbreviated to !g ds.\n\n> !game longrest\nResets your abilities and spell slots that reset after a long rest. Can be abbreviated to !g lr.\n\n> !game shortrest\nResets your abilities that reset after a short rest. Can be abbreviated to !g sr.\n\nAdd adv or dis to your command to roll with advantage or disadvantage. Add -b [bonus] to add to your checks, saves, and attack rolls, and -d [bonus] to add to your damage rolls. Finally, add -rr [number] to roll more than once.\n\nFor all commands, see: https://avrae.io/commands","created_at":"2021-07-08T10:14:43.179000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"862637819393474590","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
